===Netherlands vs Slovakia===
The [[Netherlands national football team|Netherlands]] defeated [[Slovakia national football team|Slovakia]] 2–1 on 28 June 2010 at the [[Moses Mabhida Stadium]] in [[Durban]]. The Netherlands' first goal was an excellent individual effort from [[Arjen Robben]] in the 18th minute, taking on the Slovak defence with the ball before scoring from 25&nbsp;yards. The Dutch had chances to extend their lead in the second half, with the most prominent coming when Robben cut inside on his left foot just like he did when he scored the first goal, but this time, Slovak goalkeeper [[Ján Mucha]] saved the shot going to his far post. The Slovaks also had two big opportunities to equalise but forced a save from [[Maarten Stekelenburg]] each time. The Dutch sealed their win in the 84th minute when [[Wesley Sneijder]] scored off an assist from [[Dirk Kuyt]] into an unguarded net after Kuyt got the ball past Mucha. [[Róbert Vittek]] slotted a penalty kick late in stoppage time, but it was no more than a consolation goal for Slovakia. The penalty had been awarded for a trip on him by Stekelenburg.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/world_cup_2010/matches/match_53/default.stm|title=Netherlands 2–1 Slovakia|last=Dawkes|first=Phil|date=28 June 2010|work=BBC News|access-date=2 July 2010 }}</ref> The Netherlands' win threatened to be overshadowed by [[Robin van Persie]] responding angrily to being substituted by coach [[Bert van Marwijk]]. Van Marwijk called a team meeting over the incident and later insisted that there was no residual unrest in the squad.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.google.com/hostednews/ap/article/ALeqM5ifb6j65HwUJqv7ZUNX1yDDKRdxSAD9GL1ME00|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100702064118/http://www.google.com/hostednews/ap/article/ALeqM5ifb6j65HwUJqv7ZUNX1yDDKRdxSAD9GL1ME00|url-status=dead|archive-date=2 July 2010|title=Van Marwijk calls team meeting over Van Persie|last=Corder|first=Mike|date=30 June 2010|agency=Associated Press|access-date=2 July 2010 }}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=http://soccernet.espn.go.com/world-cup/story/_/id/804507/ce/uk/&cc=3436?ver=global |title=Sneijder denies Van Persie rift |date=30 June 2010 |work=[[ESPNsoccernet]] |access-date=2 July 2010 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121021190058/http://soccernet.espn.go.com/world-cup/story/_/id/804507/ce/uk/%26cc%3D3436?ver=global |archive-date=21 October 2012 }}</ref>

