===Spain vs Portugal===
[[File:Spain and Portugal match at the FIFA World Cup 2010-06-29 7.jpg|thumb|right|[[Sergio Ramos]] of Spain tries to pass the ball to [[Fernando Torres]] as Portugal's [[Fábio Coentrão]], [[Bruno Alves]] and [[Cristiano Ronaldo]] look on.]]
[[Spain national football team|Spain]] defeated [[Portugal national football team|Portugal]] 1–0 in the [[Iberia]]n [[Local derby|derby]] to progress to the quarter-finals where they were to play [[Paraguay national football team|Paraguay]]. The match took place on 29 June 2010 at the [[Cape Town Stadium]]. Spain dominated their neighbours with a ball possession ratio of 62% and several opportunities but had to endure a pair of missed chances by the Portuguese in the first half, including one by [[Hugo Almeida]] which nearly resulted in a goal. In the second half, the Portuguese attacking threat decreased and the entry of [[Fernando Llorente]] for [[Fernando Torres]] brought new energy to the Spanish team. The only goal of the match came in the 63rd minute: [[David Villa]] picked up a brilliant pass by [[Xavi (footballer, born 1980)|Xavi]], having his first shot saved, but then lifted the rebound into the roof of the net.<ref>{{cite news |url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/world_cup_2010/matches/match_56/default.stm |title=Spain 1-0 Portugal|first=Chris|last=Bevan|work=BBC News|access-date=28 May 2011}}</ref> Post-match replays showed that the goal was scored from an offside position ({{convert|0.22|m|in|abbr=on}} according to [https://web.archive.org/web/20101213144159/http://bizoffootball.com/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=315:espn-axis-technology-new-high-speed-cameras-enhanced-graphics-for-mnf&catid=40:television&Itemid=57 ESPN axis]).<ref>{{cite web|publisher=livesoccertv.com|title=Spain's Villa, Argentine Refs send Portugal packing for deserved summer vacation|url=http://www.livesoccertv.com/news/1169/villa-and-refs-send-portugal-packing-for-deserved-summer-vacation/|access-date=11 July 2010 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Gaffer |first=The |url=http://www.worldcupbuzz.com/david-villas-goal-for-spain-against-portugal-was-offside-3d-video/ |title=David Villa's Goal for Spain Against Portugal Was Offside: 3D Video |publisher=Worldcupbuzz.com |date=30 June 2010 |access-date=1 April 2012 |archive-date=26 March 2012 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120326191529/http://www.worldcupbuzz.com/david-villas-goal-for-spain-against-portugal-was-offside-3d-video/ |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|publisher=Goal.com|title=Carvalho: Offside|url=http://www.goal.com/en/news/1863/world-cup-2010/2010/07/03/2007282/world-cup-2010-argentina-coach-diego-maradona-claims|access-date=11 July 2010 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|publisher=chelseafc.com|title=World Cup 2010: Argentina Coach Diego Maradona Claims 'Horrible' Refereeing Helped Spain Beat Portugal|url=http://www.chelseafc.com/page/WorldCupNews/0,,10268~2081498,00.html|access-date=11 July 2010 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |author=Lusitan |url=http://portugoal.net/index.php/more-portugal-news/12676-reaction-qwe-could-have-gone-furtherq |title=Reaction: "We could have gone further" |publisher=Portugoal.net |date=29 June 2010 |access-date=1 April 2012 |archive-date=22 March 2012 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120322145748/http://portugoal.net/index.php/more-portugal-news/12676-reaction-qwe-could-have-gone-furtherq |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|publisher=iafrica.com|title=Villa was offside|url=http://sport.iafrica.com/news/2513304.htm|access-date=11 July 2010|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100708210404/http://sport.iafrica.com/news/2513304.htm|archive-date=8 July 2010|url-status=dead|df=dmy-all}}</ref>

