===Argentina vs Germany===
[[File:FIFA World Cup 2010 Argentina vs Germany - Thomas Müller opening goal.gif|thumb|[[Thomas Müller]] heads in the opening goal for Germany from [[Bastian Schweinsteiger]]'s free kick.]]
On 3 July 2010, [[Germany national football team|Germany]] beat [[Argentina national football team|Argentina]] 4–0 at the [[Cape Town Stadium]] to reach the semi-finals.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://mobile.latimes.com/inf/infomo?view=SportItem&feed:a=latimes_1min&feed:c=sportsnews&feed:i=54736429|title=Germany overwhelms Argentina, 4–0, to reach World Cup semifinals|last=Jones|first=Graham L.|date=3 July 2010|work=[[Los Angeles Times]]|access-date=4 July 2010|archive-date=7 July 2010|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100707185903/http://mobile.latimes.com/inf/infomo?view=SportItem&feed:a=latimes_1min&feed:c=sportsnews&feed:i=54736429|url-status=dead}}</ref> It was the third time in the tournament that Germany had scored four goals in a match. Germany's first goal was scored by [[Thomas Müller]] in the third minute of the match with a header from a free kick taken by [[Bastian Schweinsteiger]]. Early in the second half, Argentina pressed Germany and came close to scoring on a number of occasions, but Germany hit back on a counter-attack in the 67th minute when [[Miroslav Klose]] scored into an empty goal from a pass by [[Lukas Podolski]]. Germany's third goal came from [[Arne Friedrich]] after sliding the ball inside from Schweinsteiger's pass seven minutes later, before Klose took the score to 4–0, volleying the ball into the net off a cross from [[Mesut Özil]].<ref>{{cite news|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/world_cup_2010/matches/match_59/default.stm|title=Argentina 0–4 Germany|last=Bevan|first=Chris|date=3 July 2010|work=[[BBC Sport]]|access-date=4 July 2010}}</ref> The 4–0 defeat was Argentina's biggest loss at a World Cup since 1974.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/2010-07-03/germany-defeats-argentina-4-0-to-advance-to-soccer-s-world-cup-semifinals.html|title=Germany Defeats Argentina 4–0 Led by Miroslav Klose, Moves to Semifinals|last=Bensch|first=Bob|date=3 July 2010|work=[[Bloomberg L.P.]]|access-date=4 July 2010}}</ref> Germany's coach [[Joachim Löw]] hailed his side's performance as one of "absolute class",<ref>{{cite news|url=https://news.yahoo.com/s/ap/20100703/ap_on_sp_so_ga_su/soc_wcup_argentina_germany|title=World Cup: Germany beats Argentina, 4–0|last=Armour|first=Nancy|date=3 July 2010|agency=Associated Press|access-date=4 July 2010}}</ref> but admitted the suspension of Müller for picking up a yellow card was a blow.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.google.com/hostednews/afp/article/ALeqM5iQCtQzqbSPCJu3qegJeZPiYsJlMw|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100707071932/http://www.google.com/hostednews/afp/article/ALeqM5iQCtQzqbSPCJu3qegJeZPiYsJlMw|url-status=dead|archive-date=7 July 2010|title=Germany ponder Mueller replacement|date=4 July 2010|agency=[[Agence France-Presse]]|access-date=4 July 2010}}</ref>

