==Semi-finals==

===Uruguay vs Netherlands===
[[Uruguay national football team|Uruguay]] played the [[Netherlands national football team|Netherlands]] in the first semi-final on 6 July 2010 at the [[Cape Town Stadium]]. The Netherlands won the match 3–2, thereby qualifying for the final for the first time since the [[1978 FIFA World Cup|1978 World Cup]].<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/2010-07-06/netherlands-defeats-uruguay-3-2-for-first-world-cup-final-berth-since-1978.html|title=Netherlands Defeats Uruguay 3–2, Advances to World Cup Final|last=Bensch|first=Bob|date=6 July 2010|work=[[Bloomberg L.P.]]|access-date=8 July 2010}}</ref>
Uruguay adopted a defensive posture early in the match, but were only able to hold their opponents scoreless for 18 minutes, when Dutch captain [[Giovanni van Bronckhorst]] scored from 35&nbsp;yards into the top right corner of the goal. However, the Netherlands were unable to capitalise on their lead, as [[Diego Forlán]] equalised in the 41st minute (1–1) when his shot from 25&nbsp;yards hit squarely in the middle of the goal was misjudged by goalkeeper [[Maarten Stekelenburg]] who missed it by millimetres. The Netherlands regained the lead in the second half, as a pass from [[Rafael van der Vaart]] reached Wesley Sneijder who hit it into the side-netting as Muslera dived and missed it by inches. Three minutes later, Kuyt crossed to Robben, who headed it in to make it 3–1. The Netherlands suffered a late scare when [[Maxi Pereira]], who missed a penalty against Ghana, scored a stoppage-time free kick; however, the match finished 3–2 despite desperate Uruguayan attempts to equalise.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/world_cup_2010/matches/match_61/default.stm|title=Uruguay 2–3 Netherlands|last=Bevan|first=Chris|date=6 July 2010|publisher=BBC Sport|access-date=8 July 2010 }}</ref> After the match, Uruguay coach [[Óscar Tabárez]] spoke of his pride in his team for reaching the semi-finals.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.theaustralian.com.au/sport/world-cup-2010/skippers-stunning-goal-inspires-dutch-surge-into-final/story-fn4l4sfy-1225889158800|title=Skipper's stunning goal inspires Dutch surge into final|date=8 July 2010|work=[[The Australian]]|access-date=8 July 2010}}</ref>

