===Germany vs Spain===
On 7 July 2010, [[Spain national football team|Spain]] defeated [[Germany national football team|Germany]] 1–0 in a rematch of the [[UEFA Euro 2008 Final]] (also won 1-0 by Spain) at the [[Moses Mabhida Stadium]] in [[Durban]] to progress to the [[2010 FIFA World Cup Final|World Cup Final]] against the [[Netherlands national football team|Netherlands]]. It was the first time that Spain had ever gone through to the final of the World Cup, while it was the second consecutive World Cup in which Germany had lost in the semi-finals, having lost to [[Italy national football team|Italy]] at home four years before.<ref name="APGerSpa">{{cite news |url=https://www.google.com/hostednews/ap/article/ALeqM5jtf6lamDzvPPaVA4FEbAuQeAIdLQD9GQN95O0 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100709191122/http://www.google.com/hostednews/ap/article/ALeqM5jtf6lamDzvPPaVA4FEbAuQeAIdLQD9GQN95O0 |url-status=dead |archive-date=9 July 2010 |title=Spain beats Germany 1–0 in World Cup semifinal |last=Armour |first=Nancy |date=8 July 2010 |agency=Associated Press |access-date=9 July 2010 }}</ref>

Spain had the bulk of possession throughout the match, with Germany adopting a tight defensive structure. Germany created chances on the counter-attack, but Spain also went close to scoring on numerous occasions in each half. The match was deadlocked at 0–0 until the 73rd minute, when Spain was awarded a corner. The corner, taken by [[Xavi (footballer, born 1980)|Xavi]], was met by [[Carles Puyol]], who headed the ball into the net as [[Manuel Neuer]] didn't do much to protect it to give Spain the lead. Thereafter, Spain protected its advantage and won the match.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/world_cup_2010/matches/match_62/default.stm|title=Germany 0–1 Spain|last=Fletcher|first=Paul|date=7 July 2010|publisher=BBC Sport|access-date=9 July 2010 }}</ref>

After the match, Spain's coach [[Vicente del Bosque]] praised the "excellent performance" of his team, while Germany's coach [[Joachim Löw]] predicted that Spain would win the final.<ref name="APGerSpa"/>

